{
  "about": [
    "Cursor CLI quota from end to end, one set of cases both ends are proved against. Each case is what",
    "Cursor's dashboard answered each of a runner's Cursor CLI accounts (`dashboard`, by account id: the bodies",
    "of GetCurrentPeriodUsage and GetPlanInfo, docs/cursor-runtime-contract.md §11 — Free from P0a's and",
    "Premium from P0c's recordings, Pro a monthly variant no recording has; an account missing did not get an",
    "answer), when a turn on an account met the usage limit (`limitReachedAt`), the heartbeat planUsage the",
    "runner sends for that (`planUsage`, fetchedAt left out), and what the control plane decides from it: the",
    "account a new session starts on (`startOn`, accountToStartOn), and per account until when its quota holds",
    "a run back (`blockedUntil`, planUsageBlockedUntil), whether it is reported at all (`reported`,",
    "planUsageReported) and when a run that just met its limit is retried (`resetsAt`, usageLimitResetsAt).",
    "src/runner-go cursor_usage_test.go serves `dashboard` and must send `planUsage` (its subtest named by the",
    "case's `id`); cursor-plan-usage.spec.ts reads `planUsage` and must decide the rest (its case named by `name`)."
  ],
